1
00:00:01,041 --> 00:00:03,333
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:13,791
[Chief Loyalist] Report.

3
00:00:13,791 --> 00:00:15,833
[Loyalist #1]
I believe I'm close.

4
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:18,458
I've been following a series
of exotic readings

5
00:00:18,458 --> 00:00:20,125
that look promising.

6
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:21,250
[Chief Loyalist]
I will be the judge

7
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:24,041
of what is promising or not.

8
00:00:24,041 --> 00:00:26,125
Keep me informed
of any data you uncover.

9
00:00:26,125 --> 00:00:26,958
Report.

10
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:30,291
Nothing?

11
00:00:30,291 --> 00:00:32,458
How about the rest of you?

12
00:00:32,458 --> 00:00:34,333
Are you even trying?

13
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:36,833
Her return to glory
is in our hands!

14
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:38,458
Do you understand that?

15
00:00:38,458 --> 00:00:39,916
We cannot fail!

16
00:00:39,916 --> 00:00:41,291
The Weapon of Desolation

17
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:43,125
should be releasing
massive amounts of energy

18
00:00:43,125 --> 00:00:44,250
during each creation event...

19
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:47,333
pulses so significant
they have to be traceable.

20
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:48,666
So trace them!

21
00:00:52,125 --> 00:00:53,541
You're out there

22
00:00:53,541 --> 00:00:55,875
making your little monsters,

23
00:00:55,875 --> 00:00:57,500
and we will find you

24
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,041
so you can make them for us.

25
00:01:00,041 --> 00:01:02,000
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

26
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,166
♪ So much to see ♪

27
00:01:03,166 --> 00:01:06,166
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

28
00:01:06,166 --> 00:01:07,791
♪ Together we will rise ♪

29
00:01:07,791 --> 00:01:09,416
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

30
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:10,875
♪ Together we will rise ♪

31
00:01:10,875 --> 00:01:13,000
♪ For what's right ♪

32
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:20,791
[groaning]

33
00:01:20,791 --> 00:01:21,916
[agent] What's this?

34
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:23,875
Your Mud Consumption
Supplemental Permit

35
00:01:23,875 --> 00:01:25,125
has a smudge on the corner?

36
00:01:25,125 --> 00:01:26,166
Hands on your head!
-[charging weapons]

37
00:01:26,166 --> 00:01:28,333
What's going on?

38
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:29,750
Where am I?

39
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:31,416
[groaning] Uh... actually,

40
00:01:31,416 --> 00:01:33,083
who am I?

41
00:01:33,083 --> 00:01:34,041
Hey!

42
00:01:34,041 --> 00:01:35,833
You people in suits,

43
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:38,375
you must be official
or something, right?

44
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:40,666
Sir, we are
from the Administration.

45
00:01:40,666 --> 00:01:42,291
I can honestly tell you

46
00:01:42,291 --> 00:01:45,375
we are literally as official
as it is possible to be.

47
00:01:45,375 --> 00:01:48,666
Indeed, "official"
is our one defining trait.

48
00:01:48,666 --> 00:01:49,750
[Jay] Uh, great.

49
00:01:49,750 --> 00:01:52,416
Can you officially tell me
who I am?

50
00:01:52,416 --> 00:01:53,541
[agent] Unlikely.

51
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:54,916
Our field database
only has files

52
00:01:54,916 --> 00:01:56,333
on important people,

53
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:58,333
and, uh, well,
don't get your hopes up.

54
00:01:58,333 --> 00:01:59,916
[scanner surging]

55
00:01:59,916 --> 00:02:00,916
What?

56
00:02:00,916 --> 00:02:02,375
Can that be right?

57
00:02:02,375 --> 00:02:04,125
[scanner surging]

58
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:05,958
Agent Jay Walker.

59
00:02:05,958 --> 00:02:08,458
Jay Walker, Jay Walker.

60
00:02:08,458 --> 00:02:09,500
Jay Walker.

61
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,500
Hey, this guy's... management!

62
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:17,208
Oh, uh... thanks?

63
00:02:17,208 --> 00:02:19,416
Sorry we didn't recognize you,
Agent Walker.

64
00:02:19,416 --> 00:02:21,166
Can we get you
anything else, sir?

65
00:02:21,166 --> 00:02:23,458
If this is a test,
I hope we passed, sir.

66
00:02:23,458 --> 00:02:25,750
I'm up for a promotion
in a few decades,

67
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:27,875
so if you could put
in a good word for me--

68
00:02:27,875 --> 00:02:30,500
Jay, it's you!

69
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,500
Agent Donovan!

70
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,750
Bro, I was so worried

71
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:33,833
when you didn't show up

72
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:35,416
for the inter-departmental
pickleball.

73
00:02:35,416 --> 00:02:37,250
You... know me?

74
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:39,166
Know you?

75
00:02:39,166 --> 00:02:40,625
Stop kidding around, Jay.

76
00:02:40,625 --> 00:02:42,416
You're only
my best friend ever!

77
00:02:42,416 --> 00:02:44,083
What are you doing
out here, buddy?

78
00:02:44,083 --> 00:02:45,708
What's with these clothes?

79
00:02:45,708 --> 00:02:47,708
Let's get you back
to your department.

80
00:02:49,875 --> 00:02:51,375
[Jay] This is where I woke up.

81
00:02:51,375 --> 00:02:53,583
First place
I ever remember being.

82
00:02:53,583 --> 00:02:56,000
If coming here
doesn't unlock my memories,

83
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,291
I don't know what will.

84
00:02:57,291 --> 00:02:58,750
All of us who flew
into the Merge

85
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:00,291
woke up in weird places,

86
00:03:00,291 --> 00:03:02,833
but we all kept our memories.

87
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:05,041
Why are you the only one
with amnesia?

88
00:03:05,041 --> 00:03:08,208
Maybe his brain
was less stable begin with?

89
00:03:08,208 --> 00:03:09,666
-Come on, Jay.
-[Kai yelps]

90
00:03:09,666 --> 00:03:11,500
Something here's
gotta trigger your brain.

91
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,083
Something!

92
00:03:14,083 --> 00:03:15,416
Anything...

93
00:03:19,208 --> 00:03:22,000
Frak, that's your dad?

94
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,291
Indeed!

95
00:03:23,291 --> 00:03:25,166
Frak does have the honor
of being my offspring!

96
00:03:25,166 --> 00:03:26,875
Sir Reginald Slitherbottom.

97
00:03:26,875 --> 00:03:29,125
The pleasure is all yours.

98
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:32,458
And these
are my esteemed colleagues

99
00:03:32,458 --> 00:03:34,708
in the Explorer's Club
of Ninjago!

100
00:03:34,708 --> 00:03:36,666
Johnny Courageous!

101
00:03:36,666 --> 00:03:38,125
Rowan Rockspike!

102
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:39,625
Seafoam Green!

103
00:03:39,625 --> 00:03:42,458
Last, and also least, Gweeg.

104
00:03:42,458 --> 00:03:45,291
Ha! Just pulling
your chain, Gweeg!

105
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:46,625
[grumbling]

106
00:03:46,625 --> 00:03:49,375
Huh, your names
are all surprisingly stupid.

107
00:03:49,375 --> 00:03:50,833
[all chuckling]

108
00:03:50,833 --> 00:03:52,375
I like this one.

109
00:03:52,375 --> 00:03:54,041
She's filled with vim!
[chuckling]

110
00:03:54,041 --> 00:03:55,041
Good show!

111
00:03:55,041 --> 00:03:59,125
[John] So, you're young Frak!

112
00:03:59,125 --> 00:04:01,583
Your father has spoken of you!

113
00:04:01,583 --> 00:04:02,541
Have I?

114
00:04:02,541 --> 00:04:03,833
[laughing] Remember?

115
00:04:03,833 --> 00:04:07,166
That one time we hired
that incompetent slug creature,

116
00:04:07,166 --> 00:04:09,500
you jokingly referred
to him as "Frak."

117
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:10,916
[sighing]

118
00:04:10,916 --> 00:04:12,583
Ah, yes, that I did, good sir.

119
00:04:12,583 --> 00:04:14,958
Yeah, you do have
a rather impressive memory.

120
00:04:14,958 --> 00:04:16,083
At times.

121
00:04:16,083 --> 00:04:17,791
Introduce me
to your friends, son.

122
00:04:17,791 --> 00:04:19,625
Oh, uh, Dad,

123
00:04:19,625 --> 00:04:22,208
this is Sora,
Wyldfyre, and Riyu.

124
00:04:22,208 --> 00:04:23,875
They're Ninja, just like me!

125
00:04:23,875 --> 00:04:24,875
I'm a Ninja now!

126
00:04:24,875 --> 00:04:26,791
[gasping] A Ninja?

127
00:04:26,791 --> 00:04:27,875
You don't say!

128
00:04:27,875 --> 00:04:29,125
How exciting,

129
00:04:29,125 --> 00:04:31,500
but are there any real Ninja
here with you?

130
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:33,500
Dad, we're all real Ninja

131
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,125
and Elemental Masters. I--

132
00:04:35,125 --> 00:04:36,458
Oh, yes, yes, yes,
of course you are,

133
00:04:36,458 --> 00:04:38,083
but you do know what I mean.

134
00:04:38,083 --> 00:04:39,500
The "classic" Ninja?

135
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,250
Who people
have actually heard of...

136
00:04:41,250 --> 00:04:42,541
and like.

137
00:04:42,541 --> 00:04:43,833
[grumbling]

138
00:04:43,833 --> 00:04:46,791
The original Ninja
aren't with us right now,

139
00:04:46,791 --> 00:04:49,041
but we do know all the Ninja,

140
00:04:49,041 --> 00:04:51,375
and by the way, Master Lloyd,
the Legendary Green Ninja,

141
00:04:51,375 --> 00:04:53,291
told me
I'm an excellent student.

142
00:04:53,291 --> 00:04:55,625
I'm sure you're passable
as a student, son,

143
00:04:55,625 --> 00:04:58,458
because you had
a brilliant teacher for a dad!

144
00:04:58,458 --> 00:05:00,500
[Wyldfyre and Riyu growl]

145
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,333
Any chance you're heading
back to Ninjago?

146
00:05:02,333 --> 00:05:03,708
We're in a bit of a hurry.

147
00:05:03,708 --> 00:05:05,083
Well, if you need a lift,

148
00:05:05,083 --> 00:05:08,333
there's plenty of room onboard
The Expanding Frontier...

149
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:09,708
that's the name of our airship,

150
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:12,291
and if we run out of room,
we'll just toss out Gweeg...

151
00:05:12,291 --> 00:05:14,541
preferably from 2,000 feet up!

152
00:05:14,541 --> 00:05:15,791
[all guffawing]

153
00:05:15,791 --> 00:05:16,791
[grumbling]

154
00:05:16,791 --> 00:05:19,166
Ah, just
pulling your chain, Gweeg!

155
00:05:19,166 --> 00:05:20,500
Seriously, though,

156
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,958
we'd be happy to take you all
back to Ninjago.

157
00:05:22,958 --> 00:05:23,958
Great!

158
00:05:23,958 --> 00:05:24,916
As soon as our expedition

159
00:05:24,916 --> 00:05:26,916
comes to a successful
conclusion!

160
00:05:26,916 --> 00:05:27,875
What?

161
00:05:27,875 --> 00:05:29,375
How long will that take?

162
00:05:29,375 --> 00:05:31,541
The Explorer's Club
has come here to Umbrasylvis

163
00:05:31,541 --> 00:05:33,458
following rumors
of a deadly monster

164
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,750
attacking the area.

165
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:36,958
The Club sent
its strongest members,

166
00:05:36,958 --> 00:05:38,666
but they also sent Gweeg.

167
00:05:38,666 --> 00:05:39,875
[all laughing]

168
00:05:39,875 --> 00:05:41,625
[Gweeg grumbling]

169
00:05:41,625 --> 00:05:43,541
Why do you keep
picking on that Gweeg guy?

170
00:05:43,541 --> 00:05:44,875
Worry not!

171
00:05:44,875 --> 00:05:46,791
Gweeg knows
it's all in good jest!

172
00:05:46,791 --> 00:05:47,833
He likes it!

173
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:49,583
This is bonding!
-[grumbling]

174
00:05:49,583 --> 00:05:52,791
So, you're here to protect
the town from a monster?

175
00:05:52,791 --> 00:05:54,000
Well, that's one way
of putting it.

176
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,208
Our expedition is here
to capture the monster

177
00:05:57,208 --> 00:05:59,708
so that we can bring it back
to Ninjago!

178
00:05:59,708 --> 00:06:01,208
Why would you bring
a deadly monster

179
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:02,541
back to where you live?

180
00:06:02,541 --> 00:06:04,750
To put it on display
and charge admission

181
00:06:04,750 --> 00:06:07,166
as a Wonder
of the Merged Lands, of course!

182
00:06:07,166 --> 00:06:08,583
That sounds dangerous.

183
00:06:08,583 --> 00:06:11,666
No reason to be afraid,
little lady,

184
00:06:11,666 --> 00:06:14,416
or my name
isn't Johnny Courageous!

185
00:06:14,416 --> 00:06:15,791
Which it is!

186
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:17,583
I had it legally changed...

187
00:06:17,583 --> 00:06:18,833
pending!

188
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:20,750
Dad, something's
seriously going wrong

189
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:22,000
with Elemental Powers.

190
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,541
We need to get back
to the Monastery

191
00:06:23,541 --> 00:06:24,625
as soon as we can.

192
00:06:24,625 --> 00:06:25,708
Undoubtedly!

193
00:06:25,708 --> 00:06:27,125
And I'm sure the real Ninja

194
00:06:27,125 --> 00:06:29,166
are eager
to see you again, Frak.

195
00:06:29,166 --> 00:06:31,291
There are probably swords
that need polishing,

196
00:06:31,291 --> 00:06:33,333
floors to sweep, and so forth.

197
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:35,000
Important Ninja work!

198
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,500
But in order
for the Explorer's Club

199
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,750
to return in glory,

200
00:06:37,750 --> 00:06:40,500
we'll first need
to capture our prey.

201
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,541
Tonight, we hunt monsters!

202
00:06:43,541 --> 00:06:44,750
[together] Huzzah!

203
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:46,791
Why don't you come along, son?

204
00:06:46,791 --> 00:06:48,708
Even a mediocre student
such as yourself

205
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:50,208
might, uh. learn something.

206
00:06:50,208 --> 00:06:51,666
Uh...

207
00:06:51,666 --> 00:06:52,708
[sighing]

208
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,041
Sub-Agent Prentis,
shift's over.

209
00:06:58,041 --> 00:06:59,250
What are you doing
still working?

210
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:01,291
New Merge Refugees.

211
00:07:01,291 --> 00:07:03,500
Figuring out
where to send them.

212
00:07:04,958 --> 00:07:06,500
You know my policy,

213
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:09,625
"When in doubt you might be,
send 'em to the Land..."

214
00:07:09,625 --> 00:07:11,041
"Of Lee," yes.

215
00:07:11,041 --> 00:07:12,625
I do love obeying a good rhyme,

216
00:07:12,625 --> 00:07:14,833
and there is a pair of them,
per protocol,

217
00:07:14,833 --> 00:07:16,708
but are you sure
that's where they're from?

218
00:07:16,708 --> 00:07:17,958
I'm sure it's all fine.

219
00:07:17,958 --> 00:07:18,958
Probably.

220
00:07:18,958 --> 00:07:20,541
Just keep records.

221
00:07:22,958 --> 00:07:24,083
[portal whooshing]

222
00:07:30,083 --> 00:07:32,958
[game music chimes]

223
00:07:32,958 --> 00:07:34,833
Ugh, thought he'd never leave.

224
00:07:34,833 --> 00:07:36,166
I know, right?

225
00:07:36,166 --> 00:07:38,750
Making us miss out
on valuable gaming time.

226
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:41,458
You gonna ask out
that cute Merlopian girl in HR?

227
00:07:41,458 --> 00:07:43,083
She's totally
head over gills for you.

228
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:44,416
Uh, she's nice,

229
00:07:44,416 --> 00:07:46,750
but I don't wanna date anybody.

230
00:07:46,750 --> 00:07:48,250
I can't explain it.

231
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:50,666
It's like the perfect person

232
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:52,875
is already out there somewhere.

233
00:07:52,875 --> 00:07:53,833
Out there?

234
00:07:53,833 --> 00:07:55,083
[Jay] Yeah, look,

235
00:07:55,083 --> 00:07:57,041
even though HR has shown me
my employee records,

236
00:07:57,041 --> 00:07:58,458
and I've worked here
my whole life,

237
00:07:58,458 --> 00:08:01,666
since I still
don't remember anything,

238
00:08:01,666 --> 00:08:04,375
sometimes I feel like...

239
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:06,041
Feel like what?

240
00:08:08,916 --> 00:08:10,583
You know,
I just found this picture

241
00:08:10,583 --> 00:08:12,750
from our first
permit inspection.

242
00:08:12,750 --> 00:08:16,166
The applicant tried to claim
a P-3 exemption on a CE-5!

243
00:08:16,166 --> 00:08:18,666
Ha, ha, ha!

244
00:08:18,666 --> 00:08:20,125
Sorry you don't
remember it, buddy,

245
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:21,125
but trust me,

246
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:23,333
we've had the best of times.

247
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:24,250
Yeah.

248
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:26,916
I guess we really did.

249
00:08:26,916 --> 00:08:30,875
And still undefeated
Galamorph champ, Jay Walker!

250
00:08:41,458 --> 00:08:42,416
[clanking]

251
00:08:42,416 --> 00:08:45,958
That doesn't sound
natural to me.

252
00:08:45,958 --> 00:08:47,500
[clanking]

253
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:49,333
Looks like someone
dug something up.

254
00:08:49,333 --> 00:08:50,708
Or buried something.

255
00:08:50,708 --> 00:08:51,958
[rocks tumbling]

256
00:08:56,875 --> 00:08:59,708
That's the kind of suitcase
Administration Agents use.

257
00:08:59,708 --> 00:09:00,666
[Kai gasps]

258
00:09:00,666 --> 00:09:02,250
Your old gi.

259
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:03,541
This makes zero sense.

260
00:09:03,541 --> 00:09:05,000
How could this be here?

261
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,458
"Request to bury
incriminating evidence.

262
00:09:07,458 --> 00:09:09,791
Stamped and approved."

263
00:09:09,791 --> 00:09:10,750
What does this mean?

264
00:09:13,541 --> 00:09:16,375
It means the Administration
knew I was a Ninja.

265
00:09:16,375 --> 00:09:17,583
They hid this here,

266
00:09:17,583 --> 00:09:19,916
where I woke up with no memory.

267
00:09:19,916 --> 00:09:21,208
We need to get there.

268
00:09:21,208 --> 00:09:22,416
There's someone
I need to threaten

269
00:09:22,416 --> 00:09:23,541
with intense violence!

270
00:09:24,541 --> 00:09:26,666
I mean, have a discussion with.

271
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:27,791
[Reggie] Right!

272
00:09:27,791 --> 00:09:30,375
Who's ready for a night
of monster hunting?

273
00:09:30,375 --> 00:09:31,625
[Explorers] Huzzah!

274
00:09:31,625 --> 00:09:32,833
Tonight we'll be using

275
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:35,916
these brand-new prototype
capture devices.

276
00:09:35,916 --> 00:09:37,291
Behold!

277
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,250
Aah!

278
00:09:39,250 --> 00:09:40,500
[grumbling]

279
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:41,875
Explorers!

280
00:09:41,875 --> 00:09:44,083
Split up and find the monster!

281
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,416
[Explorers] Huzzah!

282
00:09:45,416 --> 00:09:47,416
[Frak] Uh, is that a good idea?

283
00:09:47,416 --> 00:09:49,583
There's safety in numbers.

284
00:09:49,583 --> 00:09:52,750
Maybe you should go out
in groups of two or three?

285
00:09:52,750 --> 00:09:54,458
Especially since
you don't know the area

286
00:09:54,458 --> 00:09:55,625
and have no idea

287
00:09:55,625 --> 00:09:57,375
what kind of monster
you're dealing with.

288
00:09:58,833 --> 00:10:00,083
[Reggie chuckling]

289
00:10:00,083 --> 00:10:01,708
My apologies, Explorers.

290
00:10:01,708 --> 00:10:03,666
My naive son means well.

291
00:10:03,666 --> 00:10:04,958
You forget, Frak,

292
00:10:04,958 --> 00:10:06,416
the one who catches the monster

293
00:10:06,416 --> 00:10:09,750
gets the all-important
naming rights, huh?

294
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:11,375
If we went in pairs,

295
00:10:11,375 --> 00:10:13,166
who would get
to name the monster?

296
00:10:13,166 --> 00:10:15,041
It'd be madness!

297
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:17,916
Oh, don't fret, son.

298
00:10:17,916 --> 00:10:19,125
Yes, your idea was awful,

299
00:10:19,125 --> 00:10:21,208
but I do like
that you tried to participate...

300
00:10:21,208 --> 00:10:24,666
almost like
a little mini grown-up.

301
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:27,541
There's probably
no monster, right?

302
00:10:27,541 --> 00:10:28,625
Monster or not,

303
00:10:28,625 --> 00:10:30,708
these explorers
will probably get lost

304
00:10:30,708 --> 00:10:32,375
or end up in a ditch somewhere.

305
00:10:32,375 --> 00:10:33,625
We have to help.

306
00:10:33,625 --> 00:10:35,500
Why? I don't help buffoons.

307
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:36,583
Personal policy.

308
00:10:36,583 --> 00:10:38,458
[growling a question]

309
00:10:38,458 --> 00:10:39,500
Why?

310
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:41,208
'Cause helping
is the Ninja way.

311
00:10:41,208 --> 00:10:43,166
And one of them is my dad.

312
00:10:43,166 --> 00:10:44,666
Yeah, still not convinced.

313
00:10:44,666 --> 00:10:46,250
Okay, but if there's a chance

314
00:10:46,250 --> 00:10:47,625
there really is a monster,

315
00:10:47,625 --> 00:10:49,541
someone's gotta
protect this town.

316
00:10:49,541 --> 00:10:50,666
[Wyldfyre sighs]

317
00:10:50,666 --> 00:10:53,333
I guess it'd be cool
to fight a monster,

318
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:54,541
if there is one,

319
00:10:54,541 --> 00:10:56,291
which I doubt.

320
00:10:59,041 --> 00:11:02,375
[distant cat screeching,
dog barking]

321
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:09,541
Why do you let your dad
talk to you that way?

322
00:11:09,541 --> 00:11:10,541
He's my dad.

323
00:11:10,541 --> 00:11:13,000
Look, my parents
were a mess too.

324
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,166
Then you get it.

325
00:11:14,166 --> 00:11:16,166
I haven't spoken to them
in years,

326
00:11:16,166 --> 00:11:18,125
probably never will again.

327
00:11:18,125 --> 00:11:19,875
Just 'cause someone's
related to you

328
00:11:19,875 --> 00:11:21,875
doesn't mean
you have to take their abuse.

329
00:11:21,875 --> 00:11:24,500
It's called
family loyalty, Sora.

330
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:26,458
Some of us obviously
have a harder time

331
00:11:26,458 --> 00:11:29,541
just walking away from family
than you do.

332
00:11:36,291 --> 00:11:38,708
Can't imagine the same trick
we used the last time

333
00:11:38,708 --> 00:11:39,875
will work again.

334
00:11:39,875 --> 00:11:41,833
Got a new plan
for getting in there?

335
00:11:41,833 --> 00:11:43,291
Yeah, I got a guy.

336
00:11:43,291 --> 00:11:45,041
Called him as soon as
I came up with the idea.

337
00:11:45,041 --> 00:11:46,041
What guy?

338
00:11:46,041 --> 00:11:47,416
Trust me, you'll love him.

339
00:11:47,416 --> 00:11:49,291
[novelty horn honks
"La Cucaracha"]

340
00:11:50,791 --> 00:11:53,000
[brakes screeching]

341
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,750
[coughing]

342
00:11:59,541 --> 00:12:01,333
Jay!

343
00:12:01,333 --> 00:12:03,166
My guy! [laughing]

344
00:12:03,166 --> 00:12:04,916
Rapton!

345
00:12:04,916 --> 00:12:06,000
[together] Rapton?

346
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,041
[grunting]

347
00:12:09,666 --> 00:12:10,958
[chuckling]

348
00:12:10,958 --> 00:12:14,291
Aw, Rapton's thrilled
to see you, you old outlaw!

349
00:12:14,291 --> 00:12:15,750
It's been too long!

350
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:16,791
Jay hasn't seen you

351
00:12:16,791 --> 00:12:19,416
since we pulled that job
in Shintaro!

352
00:12:19,416 --> 00:12:20,625
[scoffing] Pfft!
Can you believe

353
00:12:20,625 --> 00:12:24,458
some clown paid so much
for an ugly cursed skull?

354
00:12:24,458 --> 00:12:25,458
[cackling]

355
00:12:25,458 --> 00:12:27,375
[laughing] Don't make me laugh.

356
00:12:27,375 --> 00:12:29,833
-Jay, you know this jerk?
-Jay, you know these jerks?

357
00:12:29,833 --> 00:12:31,291
Oh, you've met?

358
00:12:31,291 --> 00:12:33,500
We came when you called, Jay.

359
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,625
Whatcha need, brother?

360
00:12:34,625 --> 00:12:36,125
Gotta get in there.

361
00:12:36,125 --> 00:12:37,333
Jay's got a plan,

362
00:12:37,333 --> 00:12:39,833
but Jay needs you
to help Jay pull it off.

363
00:12:39,833 --> 00:12:41,125
How much will it cost?

364
00:12:41,125 --> 00:12:42,458
For Jay?

365
00:12:42,458 --> 00:12:43,708
Free of charge!

366
00:12:43,708 --> 00:12:44,916
[grumbling]

367
00:12:44,916 --> 00:12:46,458
Pow!

368
00:12:46,458 --> 00:12:48,333
Yeah!

369
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,666
[♪♪♪]

370
00:12:49,666 --> 00:12:52,541
Yeah! Whoo!

371
00:12:52,541 --> 00:12:53,500
[fireworks blasting]

372
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,333
Cease!

373
00:12:59,333 --> 00:13:03,083
You're breaking literally
15 different local ordinances!

374
00:13:03,083 --> 00:13:04,666
[cackling]

375
00:13:04,666 --> 00:13:06,666
We think ordinances are dumb!

376
00:13:06,666 --> 00:13:08,208
It's cool to break 'em!

377
00:13:08,208 --> 00:13:09,291
Yeah!

378
00:13:09,291 --> 00:13:10,750
[tires squealing]

379
00:13:10,750 --> 00:13:13,250
These hooligans and scofflaws
won't comply.

380
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:14,625
[firing blasters]

381
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,250
Move in!

382
00:13:20,250 --> 00:13:22,583
[♪♪♪]

383
00:13:30,416 --> 00:13:31,708
[whistling]

384
00:13:33,791 --> 00:13:35,125
[body slumping]

385
00:13:36,958 --> 00:13:40,583
Oh! Ow! Oh, no!

386
00:13:40,583 --> 00:13:42,333
[engine roaring up]

387
00:13:42,333 --> 00:13:44,791
Oh, why did we dare tangle

388
00:13:44,791 --> 00:13:48,125
with the unstoppably dapper
Administration?

389
00:13:48,125 --> 00:13:50,208
We must flee for our lives!

390
00:13:51,333 --> 00:13:52,333
[stammering]

391
00:13:55,666 --> 00:13:56,541
[engine roaring away]

392
00:13:59,583 --> 00:14:01,750
Good work, Agents!

393
00:14:01,750 --> 00:14:04,375
And the scofflaws
left a vehicle behind.

394
00:14:04,375 --> 00:14:06,166
Have it confiscated!

395
00:14:16,625 --> 00:14:18,875
[Nya] I can't believe
something Rapton did

396
00:14:18,875 --> 00:14:20,291
actually worked!

397
00:14:20,291 --> 00:14:21,541
[Kai] So where do we go now?

398
00:14:21,541 --> 00:14:23,333
[Jay] He'll probably be
in his office soon.

399
00:14:25,041 --> 00:14:26,625
[Nya] Who's "he"?

400
00:14:26,625 --> 00:14:27,708
[Kai] I stopped
understanding anything

401
00:14:27,708 --> 00:14:29,500
back when we were in a stomach.

402
00:14:33,125 --> 00:14:34,125
[screeching]

403
00:14:34,125 --> 00:14:36,000
[Wyldfyre] A real monster!

404
00:14:37,166 --> 00:14:38,500
[monster hissing]

405
00:14:40,458 --> 00:14:41,916
[panting]

406
00:14:43,208 --> 00:14:44,750
[grunting with effort]

407
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:46,750
[Frak] Come on, work!

408
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:47,791
[ground rumbling]

409
00:14:48,666 --> 00:14:50,625
[all yelping] Whoa!

410
00:14:51,916 --> 00:14:52,791
[snarling]

411
00:14:55,875 --> 00:14:59,041
[Sora gasps]
Don't let it get away!

412
00:15:01,208 --> 00:15:03,041
[monster hissing overhead]

413
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:05,958
[yelping]

414
00:15:05,958 --> 00:15:08,208
Courageous
might wanna change his name.

415
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,375
Ha ha!

416
00:15:13,916 --> 00:15:16,208
[snarling]

417
00:15:16,208 --> 00:15:17,208
[panting]

418
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:19,041
Work, powers, work!

419
00:15:19,041 --> 00:15:21,208
Aah, fine, whatever!

420
00:15:21,208 --> 00:15:22,333
H'yah!

421
00:15:22,333 --> 00:15:24,250
[screaming]

422
00:15:25,333 --> 00:15:26,333
[snarling]

423
00:15:28,208 --> 00:15:29,958
Hmm. Hup!

424
00:15:33,833 --> 00:15:34,708
Aah!

425
00:15:35,541 --> 00:15:36,958
[Frak] Dad! No!

426
00:15:40,166 --> 00:15:42,416
Oh, boy.

427
00:15:43,958 --> 00:15:45,375
Oof!

428
00:15:45,375 --> 00:15:46,375
[snarling]

429
00:15:51,041 --> 00:15:52,291
[yelping]

430
00:15:53,166 --> 00:15:54,041
[slamming]

431
00:16:03,208 --> 00:16:04,125
[snarling]

432
00:16:04,125 --> 00:16:05,333
[Riyu barks]

433
00:16:05,333 --> 00:16:08,291
[barking]

434
00:16:12,833 --> 00:16:14,666
[yelping]

435
00:16:16,041 --> 00:16:18,541
[shrieking in pain]

436
00:16:23,958 --> 00:16:25,875
[Riyu shrieks]

437
00:16:31,250 --> 00:16:32,291
[Riyu groaning in pain]

438
00:16:33,916 --> 00:16:36,333
[Sora] Come on,
powers, come on!

439
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:42,708
[Riyu shrieks]

440
00:16:44,708 --> 00:16:46,083
[panting with effort]

441
00:16:48,083 --> 00:16:49,083
[monster hissing]

442
00:16:49,083 --> 00:16:50,791
[groaning in pain]

443
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:54,291
[both] Riyu!

444
00:16:55,375 --> 00:16:58,125
Son, you tried to rescue me!

445
00:16:58,125 --> 00:16:59,333
It's what I do, Dad--

446
00:16:59,333 --> 00:17:00,958
But you only got in my way.

447
00:17:00,958 --> 00:17:04,041
I would've trapped it myself
if you hadn't shown up.

448
00:17:04,041 --> 00:17:06,166
Next time, think.

449
00:17:06,166 --> 00:17:07,250
[Riyu groans]

450
00:17:14,583 --> 00:17:16,958
[♪♪♪]

451
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,500
[snoring]

452
00:17:27,125 --> 00:17:29,708
[light switch clicking]

453
00:17:29,708 --> 00:17:31,791
[groaning] Lousy lights.

454
00:17:31,791 --> 00:17:34,250
Now I have to
requisition repairs.

455
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,208
[chair wheels spinning]

456
00:17:42,791 --> 00:17:45,166
Jay! Where have you been?

457
00:17:45,166 --> 00:17:47,250
And what's with
the hair and uniform?

458
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:49,208
You went out on that
equipment reclamation operation

459
00:17:49,208 --> 00:17:50,250
in Mysterium

460
00:17:50,250 --> 00:17:51,250
and never came back.

461
00:17:51,250 --> 00:17:52,375
Shut it, Blake!

462
00:17:52,375 --> 00:17:53,833
I know it's an act.

463
00:17:53,833 --> 00:17:56,500
My so-called best friend

464
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:59,666
with fake photos of us
as young agents together.

465
00:17:59,666 --> 00:18:00,833
Fake?

466
00:18:00,833 --> 00:18:02,125
What are you talking about?

467
00:18:02,125 --> 00:18:03,791
I got receipts.

468
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:06,000
I wanted to believe
you weren't in on it...

469
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,875
maybe you had your memories
altered too,

470
00:18:07,875 --> 00:18:09,125
but no!

471
00:18:09,125 --> 00:18:12,125
A request to bury
incriminating evidence form,

472
00:18:12,125 --> 00:18:14,708
and whose name
is on that signature line?

473
00:18:14,708 --> 00:18:15,666
Tell me.

474
00:18:15,666 --> 00:18:18,125
Agent Blake Donovan.

475
00:18:18,125 --> 00:18:20,291
So you finally figured it out?

476
00:18:20,291 --> 00:18:21,416
Took you long enough.

477
00:18:21,416 --> 00:18:23,125
Who erased my memories?

478
00:18:23,125 --> 00:18:24,208
Was it you?

479
00:18:24,208 --> 00:18:26,375
Why? Tell me why!

480
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:28,000
You don't get it.

481
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,125
There are things
you'll never understand, Jay.

482
00:18:30,125 --> 00:18:31,583
Is that so?

483
00:18:31,583 --> 00:18:35,416
Well, one thing I do understand
is what this does.

484
00:18:35,416 --> 00:18:36,916
You wouldn't.

485
00:18:36,916 --> 00:18:38,541
You wanna bet?

486
00:18:38,541 --> 00:18:39,875
Uh, what if, um...

487
00:18:39,875 --> 00:18:41,291
What if I told you

488
00:18:41,291 --> 00:18:42,708
how you could
unblock your memories.

489
00:18:42,708 --> 00:18:43,583
[Jay] How?

490
00:18:43,583 --> 00:18:45,250
33rd floor, Section A9.

491
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:46,625
Where your memories
were blocked.

492
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:49,250
There could be a way
to reverse it.

493
00:18:49,250 --> 00:18:50,916
Why should I trust you?

494
00:18:50,916 --> 00:18:53,000
Cause I'm the only hope
you have

495
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,833
of ever remembering
your real life.

496
00:18:56,125 --> 00:18:57,291
Take me there.

497
00:18:57,291 --> 00:18:58,375
No problem,

498
00:18:58,375 --> 00:19:00,083
I'll just get you
the access code, and--

499
00:19:00,083 --> 00:19:01,041
Chair! [clattering]

500
00:19:02,833 --> 00:19:04,666
So long, suckers!

501
00:19:06,625 --> 00:19:08,541
Ugh! That jerk-head!

502
00:19:08,541 --> 00:19:09,708
[typing]

503
00:19:09,708 --> 00:19:10,833
According to this,

504
00:19:10,833 --> 00:19:12,750
the 33rd floor, Section A9

505
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:15,208
is the Department
of Vacation Simulation.

506
00:19:15,208 --> 00:19:16,791
It's gotta be another lie.

507
00:19:16,791 --> 00:19:18,208
Why would a Vacation department

508
00:19:18,208 --> 00:19:20,250
have anything to do
with Jay's memory loss?

509
00:19:20,250 --> 00:19:22,375
'Cause according to
what I'm seeing here,

510
00:19:22,375 --> 00:19:25,458
they've got some
brain-accessing tech up there.

511
00:19:25,458 --> 00:19:26,666
We can't stay here.

512
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:28,458
I'm sure Blake's
reported us already.

513
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:30,333
Agents will be on us in seconds.

514
00:19:30,333 --> 00:19:33,208
-[banging]
-Freeze, enemies of bureaucracy!

515
00:19:33,208 --> 00:19:34,875
Uh, I swear,

516
00:19:34,875 --> 00:19:38,208
if this is another one
of Agent Donovan's pranks...

517
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:43,250
Aah!

518
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:45,041
[gasping]

519
00:19:47,375 --> 00:19:49,208
I was afraid that'd happen.

520
00:19:49,208 --> 00:19:50,791
I do not like elemental powers

521
00:19:50,791 --> 00:19:53,541
being all messed up like this.

522
00:19:53,541 --> 00:19:54,916
Thanks for the catch.

523
00:19:54,916 --> 00:19:56,416
Any time.

524
00:19:56,416 --> 00:19:58,333
We've been wandering for hours.

525
00:19:58,333 --> 00:20:00,416
The dragon said I'd find
the Temple of the Green Ninja

526
00:20:00,416 --> 00:20:01,750
if I was meant to.

527
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:04,000
[sighing]
Maybe I'm not meant to.

528
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,166
Maybe it's true,

529
00:20:05,166 --> 00:20:06,166
I'm too old,

530
00:20:06,166 --> 00:20:07,833
and it's too late
to do the Ritual.

531
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:10,541
Maybe you should try
meditating.

532
00:20:10,541 --> 00:20:12,750
Who are you? Me?

533
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:15,750
It's what you'd
tell me to do, isn't it?

534
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:18,750
Should follow my own advice.

535
00:20:22,791 --> 00:20:23,750
Get comfortable.

536
00:20:23,750 --> 00:20:25,833
This might take a while.

537
00:20:28,916 --> 00:20:29,916
[energy sparking]

538
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,041
I... feel something already.

539
00:20:35,041 --> 00:20:37,875
Well, good thing
I didn't get comfortable.

540
00:20:37,875 --> 00:20:40,833
Wait... this isn't
from my meditations.

541
00:20:40,833 --> 00:20:41,833
It's...

542
00:20:43,916 --> 00:20:45,500
[snarling]

543
00:20:55,833 --> 00:20:57,541
[snarling]

544
00:20:58,791 --> 00:20:59,791
Aah!

545
00:21:01,125 --> 00:21:04,833
[grunting with effort]

546
